From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:36:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] tourism: the monthly loops in top-level kernels (B3 T1,
 bit-identical)

The per-venue and per-cell loops of the once-a-month update ran in
baseline code inside the big update() closure while V8 compiled the
closure for OSR (12-73 ms on a background thread): 4-12 ms a tick at 1M
instead of 1-2. venueLoop, splatVenues, visitorsLayer (1 - exp(-sum))
and coarseBlur3 are small top-level functions now; same operations in
the same order. (The map's tourism-jit-hygiene.patch, venuePass named
venueLoop.)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KT9tXthEhyzExdUuGEecAJ
